  "is_prerecorded": false,
  "description": "The ancient festivals of Lúnasa and Lammas take place this week, commemorating the forthcoming harvest - a time for ritual play, hand-fasting, and feasts. In the Pacific Northwest, events such as the PNW Witches’ Market festival for Lammas and Lughnasadh and the Washington Midsummer Renaissance Festival mark the occasion - along with live shows from regional artists.\n\nThis week, Convergence Zone embraces upcoming live shows with new dark tides by Other, Arkham Sunset, Bridal Veil, ACTORS, and The Discussion\n\nI’ll also have ambient and space music for summer by Patricia Wolf, Pulse Emitter, Brian Eno and Beatie Wolfe, DTime, and Arkham Sunset (a twofer!)\n\nConvergence Zone arrives Tuesday nights at 8:30pm PT on 90.7 KSER-FM, 89.9 KXIR-FM, streaming around the world at kser.org or on your favorite smart speaker",
